WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.309
(zipper closing)

00:00:02.309 --> 00:00:03.936
(dramatic music)

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:04.769
- [Narrator] Pop quiz.

00:00:04.769 --> 00:00:05.769
Who is this?

00:00:09.307 --> 00:00:12.019
If you answered Olympic gold
medalist freestyle skier

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:16.949
Jonny Moseley, you are
correct. It is Jonny Moseley.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:19.011
- Hey, I'm Jonny Moseley.

00:00:19.011 --> 00:00:20.619
- [Narrator] Here's another question.

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:23.491
What exactly is Jonny
Moseley doing right now?

00:00:23.491 --> 00:00:25.240
It's strange.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.599
It's as if Jonny is figure skating

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:28.432
on skis.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.697
What you're witnessing is a rare glimpse

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:34.731
of a lost athletic art
that was once the pinnacle

00:00:34.731 --> 00:00:36.469
of freestyle skiing.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:37.560
It had judges.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.690
It had costumes.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:40.011
It had fans.

00:00:40.011 --> 00:00:41.909
It had a name.

00:00:41.909 --> 00:00:42.949
Ski Ballet.

00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:45.699
(dramatic music)

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:51.010
In the beginning, young freestyle
skiers didn't just want

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:54.880
to ski down, they wanted
to ski fun and invented

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.948
a new sport that would
eventually make it all of the way

00:00:57.948 --> 00:00:59.749
to the Olympic games.

00:00:59.749 --> 00:01:01.680
Ski ballet was born.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.931
- Yeah, it just looked like a bunch

00:01:02.931 --> 00:01:04.829
of crazy stuff on skis.

00:01:04.829 --> 00:01:06.629
- [Narrator] This is three time

00:01:06.629 --> 00:01:07.760
world champion skier Bob Howard,

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.789
a legend in ski ballet when the sport

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:11.697
was in its 1980's heyday.

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:13.840
- What they didn't know
then, we don't know now.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.610
Ski ballet is very difficult.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:17.358
I'd like to demonstrate, 
but my knees are shot

00:01:17.358 --> 00:01:19.417
so I brought in Jonny Moseley.

00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:20.850
- I'm Jonny Moseley.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:21.683
- They know.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.068
Ski ballet was a form of freestyle skiing

00:01:25.068 --> 00:01:26.800
and it had a couple of
different incorporations:

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.217
it had pole flips, spins, linking tricks.

00:01:33.851 --> 00:01:35.171
We put it all together
with rock and roll music.

00:01:35.171 --> 00:01:37.338
Early on we did some moves

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:41.611
that were basically flex tricks,
where you go off your tips.

00:01:41.611 --> 00:01:45.160
And what it is, is you flex your
tip up and you spin around.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.337
Those are pretty difficult
because you're balancing

00:01:47.337 --> 00:01:48.611
and you can hurt yourself real quickly.

00:01:48.611 --> 00:01:51.219
You can dislocate your knee in an instant.

00:01:51.219 --> 00:01:54.251
Here's Jonny doing a 720,
which is two times around.

00:01:54.251 --> 00:01:55.600
We copied this from ice skating

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.040
and it even goes to a higher level,

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.919
where it goes to a 900,
which means he spins around

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:02.240
two times and lands backwards.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.677
(crowd cheering)

00:02:04.677 --> 00:02:05.811
- [Narrator] The lights in ski ballet

00:02:05.811 --> 00:02:08.149
were never brighter than when
it was a demonstration sport

00:02:08.149 --> 00:02:11.189
in the Olympics in 1988 and 1992.

00:02:11.189 --> 00:02:14.050
But ski ballet was not
long for this world.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.531
The spotlight dimmed when
the games dropped it in 1994,

00:02:17.531 --> 00:02:21.698
and the whole sport went
fully dark not long after.

00:02:23.549 --> 00:02:26.509
- The DNA of ski ballet
is actually in everything

00:02:26.509 --> 00:02:28.339
that freestylers today, all the spins

00:02:28.339 --> 00:02:30.560
and moves you see in the
slope style and the big air.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.496
We did all that from the very beginning.

00:02:32.496 --> 00:02:34.619
That's why I teach my
students ski ballet moves.

00:02:34.619 --> 00:02:38.786
"I'm gonna do it, come to
a stop and I just pull."

00:02:40.469 --> 00:02:41.531
Oh, that hurt.

00:02:41.531 --> 00:02:42.749
- [Narrator] So the next
time you're on a chair lift

00:02:42.749 --> 00:02:44.909
and you spy Jonny Moseley down below,

00:02:44.909 --> 00:02:48.019
clad in a retro onesie and 
painting a ski masterpiece

00:02:48.019 --> 00:02:51.974
on a canvas of virgin snow,
take a moment to realize

00:02:51.974 --> 00:02:55.659
that you're glimpsing
the flight of a phoenix.

00:02:55.659 --> 00:02:57.758
A phoenix called ski ballet.

00:02:57.758 --> 00:03:00.508
(dramatic music)

